{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/925426-tablets-e-readers-and-various-library-backgrounds","id":925426,"title":"Tablets, E Readers, and various \"Library Backgrounds\"","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-07-03T11:31:25-07:00","id":925426,"title":"Tablets, E Readers, and various \"Library Backgrounds\"","content":"in this age of E readers, tablets, etc, is their a reason for anyone with a massive library of occult lore not to digitalize it, except a handful of mystical books that need some kind of mystical ink.<br /> <br /> aside from convenience and portability, it also makes it much more concealable, which makes it less likely your chantry or outpost or whatever will be harassed by the government. or technocracy, as its easier to fake &quot;Perfectly normal&quot; wheither your arcanum or hermetic mage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":1153,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","user":"Prince of the Night","date":". 07-03-2016, 06:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-04T08:38:12-07:00","id":925917,"title":"","content":"It also makes it much more stealable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-04T09:09:39-07:00","id":925929,"title":"","content":"because you could just copy everything off of a server?<br /> <br /> true...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-04T10:01:24-07:00","id":925944,"title":"","content":"Sure, you can have a virtual library. Virtual Adepts do just that, but a Hermetic will probably prefer books for their mystique (just like a lot of normal people do).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-04T10:05:02-07:00","id":925946,"title":"","content":"yes but even hermetics, or the triemere, are probaly aware of in addition to improved portability, virtual librarys give them improved concealability, not a small advantage...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-04T10:53:48-07:00","id":925979,"title":"","content":"You could have both.<br /> <br /> Concealability it's not much of an advantage, books are usualy to be read in the comodity of your sanctum, not to be ported into the fray. Since in your sanctum you have the instruments of your art, it would be normal to have some books there. I don't see much need to &quot;conceal&quot; a book, unless it's your Focus or something.<br /> <br /> In the other hand, a book uploaded online, or saved in a small and expensive apararus, it's easier to steal than a book hidden in a magicaly protected library. Even a mundane could do so. That's why important industries have their backups kept in banks, instead of merely trusting the web or having copies. And books have proven that they can last millennia (they aren't ineficient in that regard). Add to that that many mages aren't very tech savvy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-04T16:25:33-07:00","id":926140,"title":"","content":"There's also some real world evidence that people learn better from material books vs machines.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-04T16:37:48-07:00","id":926154,"title":"","content":"It's also possible for the Technocracy to invent some kind of super virus that obliterates online, digitized copies of such texts. Or to identify where they are at so they can send scout teams out to investigate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-04T17:51:50-07:00","id":926182,"title":"","content":"They most assuredly can do that, after all, one of the basic uses of Correspondence/Data it's to locate something anywhere. No shielding from that, not without magic, of course.<br /> Tech savvy mages can always counter fire with fire (the VA hold an immense online Rote library in a big digital chantry, I asume that the Technocrats do the same), mages that aren't so tech savvy have less resources to protect such data.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 07-04-2016, 08:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-06T00:54:34-07:00","id":926905,"title":"","content":"There's also another reason why a mystic Mage would want to retain physical copies of books: it pulls on Mythic Threads.<br /> <br /> For the same reason why a wizard would wear robes - even if they strictly speaking didn't need to - they might use paper and binding books to invoke Mythic Threads. People expect wizards to have old books. Magic tomes of arcane lore are a staple of legend and the popular conception of the mystic arts. And when it comes to Mages, that kind of thing reinforces their presence within the context of the Consensus. Playing to type grants a Mage more power.<br /> <br /> So while it would probably serve a practical purpose to back up one's collection of arcane lore digitally, the act of being a mystic can only be helped by retaining the books themselves.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-06T08:20:37-07:00","id":927077,"title":"","content":"and what about the Arcanum? they wind up hunted a lot, being able to carry a whole library on a Separate HD would be handy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-06T09:06:39-07:00","id":927111,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/925426-tablets-e-readers-and-various-library-backgrounds?p=927077#post927077\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">and what about the Arcanum? they wind up hunted a lot, being able to carry a whole library on a Separate HD would be handy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nope totally not them, everyone else but not the Arcanum.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-06T09:28:30-07:00","id":927124,"title":"","content":"is that supposed to be flippant? a reason you can give for that sentiment beyond &quot;Scholarship&quot; being associated with musty old books being examined by candle light?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-06T10:16:50-07:00","id":927150,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/925426-tablets-e-readers-and-various-library-backgrounds?p=927124#post927124\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">is that supposed to be flippant?</div> </div> </div> </div>Ask a stupid question, get a stupid answer......","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-06T17:58:35-07:00","id":927375,"title":"","content":"I think that it's...not necessarily a bad idea, but not very good. &quot;Having an esoteric book&quot; (or even a library) it's not grounds to be hunted, having true knowledge about the supernatural it's. Occult knowledge isn't grounds for a hunt.<br /> <br /> Now, a lot of the knowledge of the Arcanum it's spotty, and while any one of the libraries of the Arcanum posses a treasure in Occult lore, that's not necessarily the same as possesing a huge amount of true supernatural lore. This it's very important because in these conditions a digital medium would be less safe than a library.<br /> A spy would need to search an entire library of obsolete dusty tomes of occult lore to find the few true facts that a given cell may posses and are grounds for hunting them.<br /> In the other hand, a digital device it's much easier to search, imagine a Nosferatu finding your virtual library, that you forgot in a coffe, and discovering &quot;the book of Nod&quot; among your titles.<br /> Not to mention that if a mundane steals it, she may start divulging things in the net that may be best to keep hidden.<br /> <br /> Now, having a hidden database with copies of your books may be a good idea, as you can hide it into a safe, and may be easier to rescue if a vampire discovers your heaven and burns it to the ground. I can see street level operatives of the Arcanum using digital devices just because they can't get a place big and well protected to keep a library of dusty tomes while they're doing their research (or at least not without calling attention). Also, I can see it as a way of safeguard data in any Arcanum base. A database, but not a tablet!. You ain't supposed to carry this dangerous data with you.<br /> <br /> The Arcanum get's discovered a lot because supernaturals are always looking for spies and covering their tracks, not because they're always searching for people with libraries.<br /> <br /> Oh, and yeah, scholars like books. Specialy scholars that delve into classic esoteric lore. It's not just that they're equal than a digital medium for the purposses of the Arcanum, but also that they have a mystique. Aesthetical reasons are also important, after all, knowledge it's supposed to be beautiful for them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 07-06-2016, 09:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-08T17:30:20-07:00","id":928525,"title":"","content":"Well, for one, you're aware that modern e-Readers don't have the high maximum resolution and quality that a book has, right? That's going to be amplified <i>massively</i> for anyone with supernatural senses.<br /> <br /> The Tremere have Auspex as a Clan Discipline, and hence the majority of them are going to be able to see in excruciating detail and precision, which means that their grimoires can have very intricate diagrams, penmanship is a big deal, etc. At the second level, they can even see the aura of a book, and it should be possible to imprint things that can be picked up that way when writing it.<br /> <br /> Likewise, the most basic level of a Sphere is a sensory one, which means that those with Correspondence can pull off a CSI &quot;Enhance!&quot;, those with Forces can see past the visual spectrum, those with Mind can pick up what the writer <i>felt</i> when they were composing the text... etc. Likewise, the most effective books a Mage can have - Grimoires/Principia - have as part of their crafting an Adept-level Effect, so they probably can't be copy-pasted without degradation - because an ordinary electronic device can't perform rotes on its own, and that one's kind of a big deal.<br /> <br /> Can these be worked around? Yes. Of course. Literally digitizing an object into the Web, creating an enspelled Tablet as a Wonder that <i>can</i> replicate even a Grimoire, making all of your collection able to be colocated, and so on. Those take effort and resources, though; it's the sort of thing that someone specialized in that sort of thing would do, but not something everyone does just because it's slightly more convenient.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6072,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6072-quantumboost","user":"Quantumboost","date":". 07-08-2016, 08:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6072-quantumboost","name":"Quantumboost","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6072_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"590"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}